    ('june-29', 'june-29-extra-sorting', 24, 'Use It', 'sorting', '{"id":"june-29-extra-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Use It","topic":"hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","hintJa":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","explanation":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","explanationJa":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","prompt":"Sort each phrase by its language purpose.","promptJa":"各表現を目的別に分類してください。","categories":["hear","reactions"],"items":[["I heard about it yesterday.","hear"],["I’ve heard of that restaurant.","hear"],["I heard it clearly.","hear"],["Exactly. That’s what I mean.","reactions"],["For real?","reactions"],["I didn’t hear what she said.","hear"]]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('june-29', 'june-29-extra-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"june-29-extra-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","hintJa":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","explanation":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","explanationJa":"存在を知っている時は hear of。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line in the conversation.","promptJa":"会話の次に続く最も自然な一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Have you heard of the new restaurant?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「新しいレストランの名前、聞いたことある？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve heard of that restaurant.","jp":"そのレストランの名前は聞いたことがあります。"},{"id":"b","en":"I heard it clearly.","jp":"それがはっきり聞こえました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Exactly. That’s what I mean.","jp":"その通り。それが私の言いたいことです。"},{"id":"d","en":"For real?","jp":"本当に？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-29', 'june-29-extra-translation', 26, 'Use It', 'translation', '{"id":"june-29-extra-translation","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Use It","topic":"hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"音そのものを目的語にする。","hintJa":"音そのものを目的語にする。","explanation":"音そのものを目的語にする。","explanationJa":"音そのものを目的語にする。","prompt":"Translate into English: それがはっきり聞こえました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：それがはっきり聞こえました。","accepted":["I heard it clearly."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-29', 'june-29-extra-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"june-29-extra-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"reactions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"同意を強く示す。","hintJa":"同意を強く示す。","explanation":"同意を強く示す。","explanationJa":"同意を強く示す。","prompt":"Which sentence best expresses this meaning: その通り。それが私の言いたいことです。","promptJa":"「その通り。それが私の言いたいことです。」に最も合う英文はどれですか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Exactly. That’s what I mean.","jp":"その通り。それが私の言いたいことです。"},{"id":"b","en":"For real?","jp":"本当に？"},{"id":"c","en":"Click the top-right box.","jp":"右上のマスを押してください。"},{"id":"d","en":"The button is in the bottom-left corner.","jp":"ボタンは左下にあります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q1', 0, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"june-30-original-q1","type":"situation","cat":"feelings","situationQuote":{"en":"A loud noise has been going on for 20 minutes."},"prompt":{"en":"You want to say 「それがイライラする」. Which sentence is natural?","jp":"大きな音が20分続いています。「それがイライラする」と言いたい時、自然なのはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It’s annoying.","jp":"それがイライラする。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m annoying.","jp":"私は人をイライラさせる人、という意味になりやすい。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m annoyed by coffee.","jp":"コーヒーにイライラしている、という変な意味。"},{"id":"d","en":"It’s annoyed.","jp":"物がイライラしている、という不自然な形。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"The noise is the cause. Use the -ing adjective.","jp":"音が原因です。原因になるものには -ing 形を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"Use “It’s annoying” when something, someone, or a situation causes the irritated feeling.","jp":"物・人・状況がイライラの原因なら “It’s annoying.” が自然です。"},"legacyId":"q1","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q2', 1, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q2","type":"mcq","cat":"feelings","prompt":{"en":"Which sentence means 「私はイライラしています」?","jp":"「私はイライラしています」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m annoyed.","jp":"私はイライラしています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m annoying.","jp":"私は人をイライラさせます。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s annoying.","jp":"それがイライラします。"},{"id":"d","en":"I annoy.","jp":"文としてかなり不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"This is your feeling, so use -ed.","jp":"自分の気持ちなので -ed を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m annoyed” describes your feeling. Be careful: “I’m annoying” sounds like you annoy other people.","jp":"“I’m annoyed.” は自分の気持ちです。“I’m annoying.” は「私は人をイライラさせる人」という意味になりやすいので注意です。"},"legacyId":"q2","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q3', 2, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"june-30-original-q3","type":"situation","cat":"nuance","situationQuote":{"en":"You try to fix a problem, but nothing works."},"prompt":{"en":"Which feeling word fits best?","jp":"問題を直そうとしているけど、うまくいきません。どの表現が一番合いますか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m frustrated.","jp":"うまくいかず、もどかしくてイライラしている。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m delicious.","jp":"私はおいしい、なので違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s winning.","jp":"勝っている、なので違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m first half.","jp":"前半です、なので違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"This is the feeling when you cannot do something smoothly.","jp":"うまくできなくて、もどかしい時の表現です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m frustrated” is perfect when something is not working and you feel stuck or blocked.","jp":"何かがうまくいかず、もどかしくてイライラする時は “I’m frustrated.” がぴったりです。"},"legacyId":"q3","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q4', 3, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q4","type":"mcq","cat":"nuance","prompt":{"en":"Which one is stronger than “annoyed” and often means quite irritated?","jp":"“annoyed” より少し強めで「かなりイライラ」に近いのはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m irritated.","jp":"かなりイライラしている。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m easy.","jp":"簡単です、なので違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m prefer.","jp":"文法的に不自然。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m second half.","jp":"後半です、なので違います。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"This word sounds a little stronger and more uncomfortable.","jp":"少し強めで、不快感が強いイメージです。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m irritated” is a little stronger than “I’m annoyed.” It can sound more serious or uncomfortable.","jp":"“I’m irritated.” は “I’m annoyed.” より少し強めで、不快感が強い感じです。"},"legacyId":"q4","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q5', 4, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"june-30-original-q5","type":"situation","cat":"nuance","situationQuote":{"en":"You have too much work, many messages, and no rest."},"prompt":{"en":"What is the most natural feeling phrase?","jp":"仕事やメッセージが多すぎて休めません。自然な表現はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m stressed out.","jp":"ストレスで疲れている。"},{"id":"b","en":"It’s preferred.","jp":"好まれている、なので違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"Who will coffee?","jp":"文として不自然。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m annoying.","jp":"私は人をイライラさせる、になりやすい。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"This is not only anger. It includes tiredness and pressure.","jp":"怒りだけではなく、疲れやプレッシャーも入ります。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m stressed out” is natural when you feel tired, pressured, and mentally overwhelmed.","jp":"疲れ・プレッシャー・ストレスで気持ちに余裕がない時は “I’m stressed out.” が自然です。"},"legacyId":"q5","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q6', 5, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q6","type":"mcq","cat":"feelings","prompt":{"en":"Mistake Detective: Which sentence is dangerous because it changes the meaning?","jp":"ミス発見：意味が変わって危ない文はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m annoying.","jp":"私は人をイライラさせる人、という意味になりやすい。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m annoyed.","jp":"私はイライラしている。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s annoying.","jp":"それがイライラする。"},{"id":"d","en":"This noise is annoying.","jp":"この音はイライラする。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"One sentence makes YOU the cause of annoyance.","jp":"1つだけ、自分がイライラの原因になる文があります。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m annoying” often means you are the annoying person. For your own feeling, say “I’m annoyed.”","jp":"“I’m annoying.” は「私は人をイライラさせる人」という意味になりやすいです。自分の気持ちは “I’m annoyed.” です。"},"legacyId":"q6","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q7', 6, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"june-30-original-q7","type":"situation","cat":"sports","situationQuote":{"en":"Japan vs Brazil is tonight."},"prompt":{"en":"What is the most natural sports question?","jp":"今夜は日本対ブラジルです。自然なスポーツ英語はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Who will win, Japan or Brazil?","jp":"日本とブラジル、どちらが勝つ？"},{"id":"b","en":"What will win, Japan or Brazil?","jp":"チームには不自然。"},{"id":"c","en":"Who will coffee or tea?","jp":"文として不自然。"},{"id":"d","en":"Which annoyed will win?","jp":"文として不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"In sports, “who” can sound natural for teams and countries.","jp":"スポーツでは、チームや国にも who が自然に使えます。"},"explanation":{"en":"In sports conversation, “Who will win?” is natural even when the choices are teams or countries.","jp":"スポーツの会話では、チームや国に対しても “Who will win?” が自然です。"},"legacyId":"q7","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q8', 7, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q8","type":"mcq","cat":"sports","prompt":{"en":"Which sentence means 「どっちが勝つと思う？」?","jp":"「どっちが勝つと思う？」に一番近いのはどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Who do you think will win?","jp":"どっちが勝つと思う？"},{"id":"b","en":"Who do you think coffee?","jp":"文として不自然。"},{"id":"c","en":"Which do you annoying?","jp":"文として不自然。"},{"id":"d","en":"Do you prefer win?","jp":"文として不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Use “do you think” inside the question.","jp":"質問の中に “do you think” を入れます。"},"explanation":{"en":"“Who do you think will win?” is a very natural way to ask for someone’s prediction.","jp":"“Who do you think will win?” は、相手の予想を聞く自然な言い方です。"},"legacyId":"q8","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q9', 8, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q9","type":"mcq","cat":"prefer","prompt":{"en":"Which question means 「コーヒーと紅茶、どちらが好きですか？」?","jp":"「コーヒーと紅茶、どちらが好きですか？」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Do you prefer coffee or tea?","jp":"コーヒーと紅茶、どちらが好きですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Are you prefer coffee or tea?","jp":"be 動詞はいりません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Do you preferred coffee or tea?","jp":"Do の後は原形です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Who prefer coffee or tea?","jp":"この場面では不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Pattern: Do you prefer A or B?","jp":"形は “Do you prefer A or B?” です。"},"explanation":{"en":"Use “Do you prefer A or B?” to ask which one someone likes more.","jp":"AとBのどちらが好きか聞く時は “Do you prefer A or B?” が自然です。"},"legacyId":"q9","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q10', 9, 'Original Review', 'situation', '{"id":"june-30-original-q10","type":"situation","cat":"prefer","situationQuote":{"en":"A: Do you prefer coffee or tea?"},"prompt":{"en":"Choose the best complete answer.","jp":"一番自然で完成した答えを選んでください。"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I prefer coffee because it smells good.","jp":"香りがいいのでコーヒーが好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer because coffee smells.","jp":"語順と意味が不自然。"},{"id":"c","en":"I am prefer coffee.","jp":"be 動詞はいりません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Coffee prefer me.","jp":"コーヒーが私を好む、という変な意味。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Answer with “I prefer A because...”","jp":"“I prefer A because...” の形で答えます。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I prefer coffee because it smells good” gives a clear preference and reason.","jp":"“I prefer coffee because it smells good.” は、好みと理由がはっきりしていて自然です。"},"legacyId":"q10","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q11', 10, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q11","type":"mcq","cat":"compare","prompt":{"en":"Which sentence means 「冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすい」?","jp":"「冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすい」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter.","jp":"冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすい。"},{"id":"b","en":"It’s easy than play golf winter.","jp":"語順が不自然。"},{"id":"c","en":"Summer is annoying to golf.","jp":"意味が違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"I prefer winter because golf annoyed.","jp":"意味と文法が不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Use “easier to...” and “than in winter.”","jp":"“easier to...” と “than in winter” を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter” naturally compares summer and winter.","jp":"“It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter.” は、夏と冬を自然に比べています。"},"legacyId":"q11","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q12', 11, 'Original Review', 'mcq', '{"id":"june-30-original-q12","type":"mcq","cat":"flow","prompt":{"en":"Which pair means 「前半 / 後半」?","jp":"「前半 / 後半」はどれですか？"},"choices":[{"id":"a","en":"first half / second half","jp":"前半 / 後半"},{"id":"b","en":"first annoyed / second annoying","jp":"意味が違います。"},{"id":"c","en":"first win / second prefer","jp":"意味が違います。"},{"id":"d","en":"half first / half second","jp":"語順が不自然。"}],"correct":"a","hint":{"en":"Use this for games, movies, lessons, and events.","jp":"試合・映画・レッスン・イベントなどに使えます。"},"explanation":{"en":"“First half” means 前半, and “second half” means 後半.","jp":"“first half” は前半、“second half” は後半です。"},"legacyId":"q12","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q13', 12, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"june-30-original-q13","type":"order","cat":"builder","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「香りがいいのでコーヒーが好きです。」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「香りがいいのでコーヒーが好きです。」"},"words":["smells","coffee","I","good","it","because","prefer"],"correctOrder":[2,6,1,5,4,0,3],"hint":{"en":"Start with “I prefer...” and give the reason with “because.”","jp":"“I prefer...” で始めて、because で理由を言います。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural sentence is “I prefer coffee because it smells good.”","jp":"自然な文は “I prefer coffee because it smells good.” です。"},"legacyId":"q13","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q14', 13, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"june-30-original-q14","type":"order","cat":"builder","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「どっちが勝つと思う？」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「どっちが勝つと思う？」"},"words":["you","win","Who","will","think","do"],"correctOrder":[2,5,0,4,3,1],"hint":{"en":"Start with “Who do you think...”","jp":"“Who do you think...” から始めます。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural question is “Who do you think will win?”","jp":"自然な質問は “Who do you think will win?” です。"},"legacyId":"q14","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q15', 14, 'Original Review', 'order', '{"id":"june-30-original-q15","type":"order","cat":"compare","prompt":{"en":"Sentence Builder: Make 「冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすいです。」","jp":"文を組み立てましょう：「冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすいです。」"},"words":["to play golf","than in winter","It’s","in summer","easier"],"correctOrder":[2,4,0,3,1],"hint":{"en":"The pattern is: It’s easier to... in A than in B.","jp":"形は “It’s easier to... in A than in B.” です。"},"explanation":{"en":"The natural sentence is “It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter.”","jp":"自然な文は “It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter.” です。"},"legacyId":"q15","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q16', 15, 'Original Review', 'matching', '{"id":"june-30-original-q16","type":"matching","cat":"mixed","prompt":{"en":"Speed Match: Match the English phrase with the Japanese meaning.","jp":"スピードマッチ：英語と日本語の意味を合わせましょう。"},"hint":{"en":"Focus on the core meaning, not only the Japanese word order.","jp":"日本語の語順ではなく、中心の意味で考えましょう。"},"pairs":[{"en":"I’m annoyed.","jp":"私はイライラしている。","cat":"feelings"},{"en":"It’s annoying.","jp":"それがイライラする。","cat":"feelings"},{"en":"I’m frustrated.","jp":"うまくいかずイライラしている。","cat":"nuance"},{"en":"I’m irritated.","jp":"かなりイライラしている。","cat":"nuance"},{"en":"I’m stressed out.","jp":"ストレスで疲れている。","cat":"nuance"},{"en":"Who will win?","jp":"どっちが勝つ？","cat":"sports"},{"en":"Do you prefer A or B?","jp":"AとBどちらが好き？","cat":"prefer"},{"en":"first half / second half","jp":"前半 / 後半","cat":"flow"}],"legacyId":"q16","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 8),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q17', 16, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q17","type":"typing","cat":"feelings","promptJP":"「私はイライラしています。」","accepted":["I''m annoyed","I am annoyed"],"hint":{"en":"Your feeling = -ed.","jp":"自分の気持ちは -ed です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I’m annoyed” describes your feeling.","jp":"“I’m annoyed.” は自分の気持ちを表します。"},"legacyId":"q17","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q18', 17, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q18","type":"typing","cat":"feelings","promptJP":"「それはイライラします。」","accepted":["It''s annoying","It is annoying"],"hint":{"en":"The thing is the cause = -ing.","jp":"原因になるものは -ing です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“It’s annoying” describes the thing or situation that causes the feeling.","jp":"“It’s annoying.” は、イライラさせる物・状況を表します。"},"legacyId":"q18","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q19', 18, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q19","type":"typing","cat":"sports","promptJP":"「日本とブラジル、どちらが勝つと思う？」","accepted":["Who do you think will win Japan or Brazil","Who do you think will win, Japan or Brazil","Who will win Japan or Brazil","Who will win, Japan or Brazil"],"hint":{"en":"Use “Who will win...?” or “Who do you think will win...?”","jp":"“Who will win...?” または “Who do you think will win...?” を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"In sports, “who” can naturally refer to teams or countries.","jp":"スポーツでは、チームや国にも “who” が自然に使えます。"},"legacyId":"q19","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q20', 19, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q20","type":"typing","cat":"prefer","promptJP":"「コーヒーと紅茶、どちらが好きですか？」","accepted":["Do you prefer coffee or tea"],"hint":{"en":"Pattern: Do you prefer A or B?","jp":"形は “Do you prefer A or B?” です。"},"explanation":{"en":"“Do you prefer coffee or tea?” is natural and clear.","jp":"“Do you prefer coffee or tea?” は自然で分かりやすい質問です。"},"legacyId":"q20","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q21', 20, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q21","type":"typing","cat":"prefer","promptJP":"「香りがいいのでコーヒーが好きです。」","accepted":["I prefer coffee because it smells good"],"hint":{"en":"Use “I prefer coffee because...”","jp":"“I prefer coffee because...” を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“I prefer coffee because it smells good” gives both preference and reason.","jp":"“I prefer coffee because it smells good.” は、好みと理由を両方言えます。"},"legacyId":"q21","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-original-q22', 21, 'Original Review', 'typing', '{"id":"june-30-original-q22","type":"typing","cat":"compare","promptJP":"「冬より夏の方がゴルフしやすいです。」","accepted":["It''s easier to play golf in summer than in winter","It is easier to play golf in summer than in winter"],"hint":{"en":"Use “easier to play golf in summer than in winter.”","jp":"“easier to play golf in summer than in winter” を使います。"},"explanation":{"en":"“It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter” is the clean comparison sentence.","jp":"“It’s easier to play golf in summer than in winter.” がきれいな比較の文です。"},"legacyId":"q22","section":"Original Review","isOriginal":true}'::jsonb, true, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-listen-choice-1', 22, 'Listen & Speak', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"june-30-extra-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"-ed は人の気持ち。","hintJa":"-ed は人の気持ち。","explanation":"-ed は人の気持ち。","explanationJa":"-ed は人の気持ち。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence you hear.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて、聞こえた英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’m annoyed by the noise.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m annoyed by the noise.","jp":"その音にイライラしています。"},{"id":"b","en":"The noise is annoying.","jp":"その音はイライラさせます。"},{"id":"c","en":"I prefer tea because it’s lighter.","jp":"軽い味なので紅茶の方が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Who do you think will win?","jp":"誰が勝つと思いますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('june-30', 'june-30-extra-listen-choice-2', 23, 'Listen & Speak', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"june-30-extra-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"-ing は原因の性質。","hintJa":"-ing は原因の性質。","explanation":"-ing は原因の性質。","explanationJa":"-ing は原因の性質。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence you hear.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて、聞こえた英文を選んでください。","audioText":"The noise is annoying.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The noise is annoying.","jp":"その音はイライラさせます。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer tea because it’s lighter.","jp":"軽い味なので紅茶の方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"Who do you think will win?","jp":"誰が勝つと思いますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"This exercise is easier than the last one.","jp":"この練習は前のものより簡単です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
